WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.729 --> 00:00:15.329
Many of you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.329 --> 00:00:19.560
still look back on your failures.
And you are letting it define who you are.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.420
How amazing is that he did not&nbsp;
let his failures define him.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:45.240
But God chose to use him and God&nbsp;
has a purpose for you as well.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:08.100
We do not have stress - worry -&nbsp;
anxiety - because our trust is in God.

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:20.040
Hey guys,
Why are some men so resilient?&nbsp;

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:27.600
It looks like everything they try to do&nbsp;
- to accomplish - is just successful.&nbsp;

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.760
Why is that?
What makes them different from other men?&nbsp;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:40.440
In my new book, Bold Pursuit, I said the&nbsp;
difference between success and failure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:46.620
is often a matter of perspective and perseverance.
And I'm going to talk about this a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.920
bit more throughout the video.
And when we turn to the Bible:

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.420
[2 Chronicles 15:7]

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:10.020
The reason why so many men give up&nbsp;
easily is because they believe a lie.&nbsp;

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:13.560
They believe that every setback is a failure.&nbsp;

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:20.040
And they assume that the problem is them.
That they are a failure.&nbsp;

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:24.960
The truth is that every setback&nbsp;
is a learning experience.&nbsp;

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:32.040
It can make you wiser if you let it.
You see, setbacks are there.&nbsp;

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.720
They're going to happen&nbsp;
whether you like it or not.&nbsp;

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:37.260
It's just part of life.
The question is, what do you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:41.100
do with it - and about it?
C.S. Lewis said:&nbsp;

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:55.920
You see, you need to change the way that&nbsp;
you think about trials and tribulations.&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.740
And failures.
Especially if you're a Christian.&nbsp;

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:04.680
That they are there to test you, that you need&nbsp;
to learn from it, knowing, alright, this is what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:10.440
happened when I did this, so I'm gonna change the&nbsp;
way I do this if this is going to happen again.&nbsp;

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:16.860
So it improves you as a man.
In fact, the more you fail, the more you grow.&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.700
Why?
Because if you learn from it - it changes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:24.600
the way you think and do certain things.
And that is how you improve.&nbsp;

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:27.780
Albert Einstein said:&nbsp;

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.200
You see, failure teaches us&nbsp;
perseverance, to keep on trying.&nbsp;

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.840
Going, going at it.
Learning from our failures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:50.220
until finally we made it.
We have achieved success.&nbsp;

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:55.620
This wisdom is nothing new.
Solomon wrote about it thousands of years ago.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:56.700
[Proverbs 24:16]

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:16.980
You see, that is how true reborn Christians&nbsp;
are different from the rest of the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:23.100
Because we will always have the right&nbsp;
perspective and perseverance living in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:28.680
righteousness, according to God's will.
Because we live through the Spirit in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.400
the middle of failure.
And you see, James said:

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:33.960
[James 1:2-4]

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:04.620
This means we will never give&nbsp;
up, and we can easily handle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:09.000
failures if we handle it through the&nbsp;
power of the Spirit that is in us.&nbsp;

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:15.240
Never having stress, or anxiety about&nbsp;
it, but if you do it through the flesh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:16.920
you will always worry.
Have stress.&nbsp;

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:20.400
Because you do not fully trust God.
And Paul also says:

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:21.000
[Romans 5:3-5]

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:57.240
And this is how we, as men in Christ, reborn&nbsp;
Christians, can also show the world that we are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:01.500
different in a way that we handle difficult times.
Our trials and tribulations.&nbsp;

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:11.280
Showing that we do not have stress - worry&nbsp;
- anxiety - because our trust is in God.&nbsp;

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:15.180
We don't have self-confidence,&nbsp;
we have God confidence.&nbsp;

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:20.700
We show them how we deal with failures,&nbsp;
with this immense inner strength that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:27.720
we know does not come from ourselves but it&nbsp;
comes from God, who created heaven and earth.&nbsp;

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:36.000
But if you act in the flesh, just in your soul&nbsp;
level with your own emotions, your own intellect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:40.020
your own will, it'll do the opposite.
Because then you look just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:45.840
like the rest of the world.
And if you act in the flesh, you will fail.&nbsp;

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:51.240
And that kind of failure is not good.
In my new book I gave this example:

00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.280
[Matthew 26:69-75]

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:19.380
You see, instead of telling the truth&nbsp;
and facing the consequences, Peter lied.&nbsp;

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:25.560
He denied even knowing Jesus.
He didn't just do it once - he did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:31.980
it three times - he had three opportunities to do&nbsp;
the right thing and he failed all three of them.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:42.420
After his third denial, Peter felt intense guilt&nbsp;
and shame and he repented for what he had done.&nbsp;

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:47.400
He learned from his mistake.
Then he did something else.&nbsp;

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.080
He showed up.
He didn't hide.&nbsp;

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:51.780
He didn't let his embarrassment get to him.&nbsp;

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:56.400
He didn't worry what other people said about&nbsp;
him behind his back or in front of him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.540 --> 00:08:03.420
When the disciples got it again, Peter showed up.
When he heard that Jesus's tomb was empty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:06.180
he showed up there too.
As fast as he could.&nbsp;

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:12.720
Peter persevered.
He refused to let his failure define him.

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:20.880
You see, God chose Peter to lead the church.
How amazing is that.&nbsp;

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:28.500
He did not let his failures define him.
Many of you still look back on your failures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:34.680
and you are letting it define who you are.
Peter overcame it and led the church - a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:41.940
normal fisherman - but God chose to use&nbsp;
him and God has a purpose for you as well.&nbsp;

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:46.440
If God calls you to do something,&nbsp;
He knows you can do it.&nbsp;

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:51.300
And He will equip you with what you need&nbsp;
to accomplish His will for your life.&nbsp;

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:58.380
You see, that's the difference between men&nbsp;
who are spiritually mature - who walk with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:03.300
God - because they act in the will of God.
And that is why God's blessing is on them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:06.900
and it seems like they are just&nbsp;
successful in everything that they do.&nbsp;

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:10.140
They don't have self-confidence,&nbsp;
they have God confidence,&nbsp;

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:14.220
And that is why they never&nbsp;
give up no matter what they do.&nbsp;

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:18.300
They know that God has their back&nbsp;
and they walk within His will.&nbsp;

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:23.160
God says, do this and they do it.
They know that God will keep His word.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:25.680
[Galatians 6:9]

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:45.120
Now most of you who worked really hard for&nbsp;
what you have, walking within the will of God,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:55.500
going through very tough times - you know most&nbsp;
of all that success tastes a lot sweeter when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:58.620
you went through hardships.
And when you persevered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:03.660
until the end, through failure.
If you put God first in everything that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:10.740
you do, then you know the good and the bad -
it will work together for good towards you.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:13.500
[Romans 8:28]

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:38.700
Now, if some of you are in this failure state,&nbsp;
make sure that what you're trying to attempt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.460
is the will of God for you.
Because if it is, it will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:47.040
be successful, even if it's hard at times.
You still know that you will continue and endure.&nbsp;

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:50.520
So if that's where you are - you're&nbsp;
fighting through the Spirit - you're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:54.300
not giving up. You're enduring.
You're battling this day-in/day-out.&nbsp;

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:59.640
Then you always need to remember&nbsp;
this while you are fighting.&nbsp;

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:02.520
Through the power of the&nbsp;
Spirit, remember this, always:

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:03.960
[Romans 12:12]

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:22.980
Now, if you want to grow faster, understanding&nbsp;
what it means to have God confidence and not just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:29.220
self-confidence, if you want to grow spiritually&nbsp;
stronger as a man, then please get my new book.&nbsp;

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:36.540
It's called Bold Pursuit, a 90-day&nbsp;
devotional for men seeking the heart of God.&nbsp;

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:39.900
You can get the link to the book&nbsp;
in the video description below.&nbsp;

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:44.400
And also on our website.
Before you go, always remember this.&nbsp;

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:51.540
Life is short, so don't waste yours.
Bye guys.

